  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "G \\text{ triangle-free},\\ |E(G)| \\ge \\left\\lfloor n^2/4 \\right\\rfloor - o(n^2)\n\\implies G \\text{ is } o(n^2)\\text{-close to } K_{\\lfloor n/2\\rfloor,\\lceil n/2\\rceil}.",
    "plain": "Mantel's theorem says a triangle-free graph on n vertices has at most ⌊n²/4⌋ edges, with equality only for the balanced complete bipartite graph. The stability strengthening (Erdős–Simonovits) says this extremal example is essentially unique even approximately: any triangle-free graph whose edge count is within o(n²) of the maximum can be turned into the balanced complete bipartite graph K_{⌊n/2⌋,⌈n/2⌉} by adding/deleting only o(n²) edges. The goal is to formalize this structural statement.",
